    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a concentrated focus on high-volume opportunities atop the order, as our offensive efficiency relies on three primary catalysts. **Sam Antonacci** represents our strongest play with a score of 54.46; despite a neutral park environment, his placement in the leadoff spot against the mid-tier xERA of 4.04 from Blubaugh provides the best projected return for our categories. **Jackson Merrill** follows closely at 52.97; while he faces a slight penalty for the platoon disadvantage against Boyd, his foundational output and favorable 5-hole protection keep his ceiling high. Meanwhile, **Miguel Vargas** earns the nod at 1B with a 50.15 score, buoyed by a strong 0.378 xwOBA that suggests he is well-positioned to capitalize on a moderate matchup.\n\nStrategic rotation remains difficult today given that core studs like **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** are all inactive due to scheduled team off-days. With **Luis Robert Jr.** sidelined on the IL, our bench depth is primarily composed of prospects and specialists. **Drake Baldwin** and **Heliot Ramos** round out the active starters at 48.14 and 47.81 respectively. **Drake Baldwin** specifically benefits from the leadoff bump, which offsets the difficulty of facing a sharp 3.06 xERA from Luzardo. While the rest of our depth\u2014including **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**\u2014did not reach the starting threshold, the optimizer remains ready to pivot if late lineup changes shift the value for fringe options like **Nasim Nunez** or **Jacob Wilson**. We are monitoring the weather closely; while there are no immediate alerts, the scarcity of stolen bases in this 5x5 format means we will be watching **Sam Antonacci** closely to see if he can exploit any defensive lapses in the Blubaugh matchup.",
